00:42:50.670 --> 00:42:52.470
That's not really
interesting yet.

00:42:52.470 --> 00:42:55.650
The next interesting
part is yet another AI.

00:42:55.650 --> 00:42:59.950
We wanted to categorize to
content within the patent.

00:42:59.950 --> 00:43:02.640
So by scanning
through the content,

00:43:02.640 --> 00:43:05.520
being able to parse the
different sentences,

00:43:05.520 --> 00:43:09.210
being able to draw semantic
meaning from the corpus

00:43:09.210 --> 00:43:13.800
into text, we're able to
determine what is the category

00:43:13.800 --> 00:43:16.470
or what is the content
for this patent.

00:43:16.470 --> 00:43:19.590
So right here in my
demo, I only created

00:43:19.590 --> 00:43:21.090
three different categories.

00:43:21.090 --> 00:43:23.340
But this can be
as many categories

00:43:23.340 --> 00:43:26.620
as you need for your
business domain.

00:43:26.620 --> 00:43:31.290
And again, I only have to
train the model with very, very

00:43:31.290 --> 00:43:35.400
few samples in order to get this
kind of accuracy and precision

00:43:35.400 --> 00:43:36.763
in my model.

00:43:36.763 --> 00:43:38.430
So what this is telling
me, for example,

00:43:38.430 --> 00:43:42.030
is every time when I run a
model, when I invoke a model,

00:43:42.030 --> 00:43:48.660
I would be able to get a
probability on whether this

00:43:48.660 --> 00:43:52.670
is a pattern relating to
medical tech, cryptocurrencies,

00:43:52.670 --> 00:43:55.860
or computer vision.

00:43:55.860 --> 00:43:58.520
So given that we
know the content,

00:43:58.520 --> 00:44:01.280
and then we want to extract
[INAUDIBLE] entities.

00:44:01.280 --> 00:44:03.980
This is pretty hard to do.

00:44:03.980 --> 00:44:07.180
Google has some
free trained APIs

00:44:07.180 --> 00:44:12.740
to extract out common entities
like objects, names, landmarks,

00:44:12.740 --> 00:44:13.670
et cetera.

00:44:13.670 --> 00:44:16.470
But not really specific
to patent documents.

00:44:16.470 --> 00:44:20.360
So this is where we'll also use
AutoML to fine tune the model

00:44:20.360 --> 00:44:22.980
and extract out only the
information that I want.

00:44:22.980 --> 00:44:25.880
So remember, this isn't
trivial because we

00:44:25.880 --> 00:44:29.790
have different languages
for our patents

00:44:29.790 --> 00:44:32.340
and we have different formats.

00:44:32.340 --> 00:44:36.080
So the positioning
of the information

00:44:36.080 --> 00:44:39.500
might be different among
all the patents you have.

00:44:39.500 --> 00:44:43.720
With the AutoML, that's
within the solution.

00:44:43.720 --> 00:44:47.390
We are able to fine tune
and extract the exact entity

00:44:47.390 --> 00:44:50.660
that we need with a pretty
high accuracy for most

00:44:50.660 --> 00:44:53.560
of the fields.

00:44:53.560 --> 00:44:57.000
And then lastly, we want
to draw it down in box.

00:44:57.000 --> 00:45:01.210
Again, this is very important
to understand illustration

00:45:01.210 --> 00:45:03.110
of the invention itself.

00:45:03.110 --> 00:45:05.950
So the object
detection technology

00:45:05.950 --> 00:45:09.430
will basically
identify any objects

00:45:09.430 --> 00:45:10.840
that you want to identify.

00:45:10.840 --> 00:45:13.570
So let's say if there are
multiple objects here,

00:45:13.570 --> 00:45:17.230
